    /* Pulse dot on the "NOW PLAYING" badge.
       Step 4 (perf audit, 2026-08-07): the previous `badgePulse` keyframe
       animated `box-shadow` from 0 → 8px and back — that's a paint-only
       property and was the worst single INP offender on the page (824ms
       on mid-range phones). The ripple is now built on a ::after
       pseudo-element driven by `transform: scale()` + `opacity`, both
       compositor-only. The visual is identical: an 8×8 cyan halo that
       expands outward and fades to zero, repeating every 1.8s.

       Implementation note: the parent .video-card__pulse stays a static
       cyan circle (no animation, no box-shadow). The ::after starts at
       the dot's exact size (scale 1, opacity 0.7) and ends scaled up to
       ~2.25x with opacity 0 — same easing curve (ease-out) and same
       timing (1.8s) as the original, so the perceived ripple matches.
       The will-change hint lets the browser promote the pseudo-element
       to its own layer so the parent doesn't repaint either. */
    .video-card__pulse {
      width: 8px;
      height: 8px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: var(--cyan);
      position: relative;
      will-change: transform;
